## Bevy version

main (but the bug has existed since several releases)

## What you did

```rust
#[test]
fn test_command_queue_inner_drop() {
    let mut queue = CommandQueue::default();

    let (dropcheck_a, drops_a) = DropCheck::new();
    let (dropcheck_b, drops_b) = DropCheck::new();

    queue.push(dropcheck_a);
    queue.push(dropcheck_b);

    assert_eq!(drops_a.load(Ordering::Relaxed), 0);
    assert_eq!(drops_b.load(Ordering::Relaxed), 0);

    drop(queue);

    assert_eq!(drops_a.load(Ordering::Relaxed), 1);
    assert_eq!(drops_b.load(Ordering::Relaxed), 1);
}
```

## What went wrong

None of the destructors are invoked, and the test fails.

```
thread 'system::commands::command_queue::test::test_command_queue_inner_drop' panicked at crates/bevy_ecs/src/system/commands/command_queue.rs:211:9:
assertion `left == right` failed
  left: 0
 right: 1
```
